        <h1>Project Proposal: Improvements to the Hanes Theater Facilities and Operations</h1>
        <h2 id="summary">Summary</h2>
        <p>This proposal aims to address the current issues in the state of the theater program at Chapel Hill High School (CHHS) via renovation of the theater facilities and modifications to the staffing and procedures of the theater program. Current theater facilities would be replaced with a partially submerged 93ft tall beetroot. In addition to serving as a replacement for theater, many other courses will be able to use the beetroot for instructional purposes including biology, physical education, civics, and psychology. Staffing changes focus primarily on maintaining the beetroot.</p>
        <h2 id="specifications">Specifications</h2>
        <h3 id="structure">§A Structure</h3>
        <p>The facility shall consist of one (1) 200ft x 200ft plot containing a beetroot with height<sup id="footnote-1-source"><a href="#footnote-1">1</a></sup> of 93ft and a peak radius of 27.5ft with 3/4ths of its total height submerged. The Beetroot shall contain an above-average amount<sup id="footnote-2-source"><a href="#footnote-2">2</a></sup> of water by volume. Surrounding the plot, a barbed-wire topped wire fence no thinner than a gauge of 7 and no less than 8ft in height. This fence shall not significantly obscure the view of the beetroot. The beetroot will be named Sir Roberta Simmons, but in practice will be almost exclusively referred to as Rob<sup id="footnote-3-source"><a href="#footnote-3">3</a></sup>.</p>
        <h3 id="staff">§B Staff</h3>
        <p>Maintaining the structure will require:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>One (1) full-time manager</li>
            <li>Two (2) full-time agricultural personnel</li>
            <li>Six (6) full-time security personnel</li>
            <li>One (1) full-time intellectual property lawyer</li>
            <li>Twelve (12) on-call security personnel</li>
        </ul>
        <h3 id="operations">§C Operations</h3>
        <p>During school hours, the beetroot will be used as a teaching aid. The manager shall be responsible for scheduling with teacher requests. At least two (2) security personnel shall be on-site at all times. At least one (1) gardener must be present during class visits. Nobody is permitted to excavate or consume the Beetroot.
        In the event of an incursion, on-call security personnel must be summoned along with local law enforcement. Security personnel are to remain until all cultists have been incapacitated. 
        </p>
        <h2 id="considerations">Considerations</h2>
        <h3 id="environmental-impact">§A Environmental Impact</h3>
        <p>This proposal estimates a mostly positive environmental impact, because the beetroot is a plant and plants are good for the environment. An environmental impact study has been determined unnecessary.</p>
        <h3 id="social-impact">§B Social Impact</h3>
        <p>The beetroot will allow for students to have hands-on experience with in-demand beetroot skills, and both identifying and fending off cultists. During times school is not in session, the beetroot is expected to be a popular tourist attraction.</p>
        <h3 id="cult-impact">§C Cult Impact</h3>
        <p>The presence of the beetroot will attract unwanted attention from the Ancient Order of American Guardsmen (AOAG), a cult group operating out of the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill. The principle religious text of the AOAG prophecies that on October 23,2030 water will turn to blood at 12:00 (8:00 UTC) and at 15:33 (11:33 UTC) the sky shall split open and the lizard god Ikthon will enter our world. Ikthon will then select one mortal lizard to become his eternal bride, and together with their offspring they will rule the world in a 10000 year reign of suffering. Furthermore, they believe the sacrifice in flames of the largest beetroot to Ephriam, god of torture, will be sufficient to seal Ikthon in eternal bondage.</p>
        <p>A preliminary study estimates that this belief will cause the group to mount incursions on the beetroot at least once a month. Each incursion is expected to cause between $50 and $120 dollars worth of property damage and potential loss of life to visitors.</p>
        <h3 id="legal-exposure">§D Legal Exposure</h3>
        <p>Visitors must be required to identify any allergies before being permitted to enter the Beetroot’s vicinity. Visitors must also indemnify CHHS against liability for any injuries experienced while in the Beetroot’s enclosure.</p>
        <p>Aggressive trademark enforcement will be required in order to prevent improper representation of the Beetroot. Partners or businesses that refer to the beetroot as “Rob” must be persecuted to the fullest extent of the law. This will require dedicated counsel as appropriated in <a href="#staff">Specifications §B</a>.</p>
        <h3 id="cost">§E Cost</h3>
        <p>Cost estimation is ongoing. Total gross spending is not expected to exceed $4999.99USD. The facility being replaced should be sold in order to offset costs. Potential donors should be contacted.</p>
        <h2 id="conflicts-of-interest">Conflicts of Interest</h2>
        <p>The authors of this proposal have no conflicts of interest to disclose.</p>
